            "review_title": "Review at La Vita Bakery",
            "review_text": "Xpatxplorer\nNew Delhi, India811 contributions\n0\nSmall but does the job!\nMay 2019 • Solo\nLa Vita Bakery\nA cute little place with really good bread and cakes ( I haven’t tried but look good). The high fiber grain bread is what I like to pick. It has really good texture and tastes delicious as a toast with butter or as a sandwhich. It comes in two sizes priced at 75,000 and 95,000. The larger one is better for a sandwhich.The takesum bread is supposed to be charcoal\nand really healthy. If you are looking for Pita they will custom make it for you. I am sure they will be willing to custom make other things as well. I remember someone giving in a request for a multigrain pizza base. Easy to become a regular customer.\nRead more\nWritten May 13, 2019",
